<section class="py-20 px-6 lg:px-20">
    <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto space-y-14">
        <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
            Marigold Signature respects the intellectual property rights of others and expects the users of our website and services
            to do the same. This page explains how to report alleged copyright, trademark, or design infringement relating to content
            on our website or to custom products produced for our clients. We respond to clear notices of alleged infringement
            promptly and in accordance with applicable law.
        </p>

        <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">1. Respect for Intellectual Property</h2>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-4">All content on our website — including text, graphics, logos, product photography, designs, software, and code — is protected by copyright, trademark, and other intellectual property laws. We expect our clients to hold or be authorised to use any artwork, logos, or designs they submit for customisation. We may refuse or discontinue production of any order that we reasonably believe infringes third-party rights.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">2. Copyright Infringement Notices</h2>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-4">If you believe that content on our website infringes a copyright you own or control, you may submit a takedown notice. Your notice must be sent to our designated contact and must include the information listed in Section 4 below.</p>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Upon receiving a complete and valid notice, we will review the claim, remove or disable access to the allegedly infringing content, and notify the affected party. We may forward a copy of the notice to the affected party and, where required, to the relevant authorities.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3. Trademark &amp; Design Infringement Notices</h2>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-4">If you believe a trademark or registered design is being used without authorisation on our website or in products we produce, please submit a notice including the information in Section 4. We will investigate the claim and take appropriate action, which may include removing the content or ceasing production of the affected custom order.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">4. Information Required in a Notice</h2>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-4">To help us act quickly and accurately, every notice must include the following:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
                <li><strong class="text-white">Identification of the IP right</strong> — the specific work, trademark, or design claimed to be infringed, including registration numbers where available.</li>
                <li><strong class="text-white">Location of the infringing content</strong> — the exact URL(s) or a description sufficient to locate the content on our website or the order/product concerned.</li>
                <li><strong class="text-white">Proof of ownership or authority</strong> — a statement that you own or control the rights, or are authorised to act on behalf of the rights holder, with supporting documentation.</li>
                <li><strong class="text-white">Your contact details</strong> — full legal name, company name (if applicable), email address, postal address, and telephone number.</li>
                <li><strong class="text-white">Good faith declaration</strong> — a statement that you believe, in good faith, that the disputed use is not authorised by the rights holder, its agent, or the law.</li>
                <li><strong class="text-white">Accuracy declaration</strong> — a statement, made under penalty of perjury where applicable, that the information in the notice is accurate and that you are the rights holder or authorised to act on their behalf.</li>
                <li><strong class="text-white">Signature</strong> — a physical or electronic signature of the rights holder or authorised representative.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">5. How to Submit a Notice</h2>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-4">Send your notice to our designated intellectual property contact:</p>
            <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--card)] border border-[var(--border)] p-6 space-y-3 text-sm">
                <p class="text-[var(--text-primary)]"><strong>Designated Agent:</strong> Intellectual Property Compliance</p>
                <p class="text-[var(--text-primary)]"><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:ip@marigoldsignature.com" class="text-[var(--gold)] hover:underline">ip@marigoldsignature.com</a></p>
                <p class="text-[var(--text-primary)]"><strong>Company:</strong> Marigold Signature Nigeria Limited</p>
                <p class="text-[var(--text-primary)]"><strong>Subject line:</strong> Please use "IP INFRINGEMENT NOTICE" for priority handling.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mt-4">We will acknowledge receipt and respond within a reasonable time, typically within 5–10 business days.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">6. Counter-Notices</h2>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-4">If content you posted or produced was removed or disabled as a result of a notice and you believe the removal was a mistake or misidentification, you may submit a counter-notice. The counter-notice must include:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
                <li>Identification of the content removed or disabled and where it previously appeared.</li>
                <li>A statement, made under penalty of perjury where applicable, that you have a good faith belief the removal was a mistake or misidentification.</li>
                <li>Your name, address, and telephone number, and a statement consenting to the jurisdiction of the courts for your location.</li>
                <li>Your physical or electronic signature.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mt-4">Upon receipt of a valid counter-notice, we may restore the content, subject to our legal obligations and the rights holder's ability to pursue the claim in court.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">7. Repeat Infringer Policy</h2>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">We maintain a policy of terminating accounts and refusing service to users who repeatedly submit or produce content that infringes the intellectual property rights of others. Factors considered include the number and severity of verified infringement claims and whether the user has made knowingly false claims.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">8. Good Faith &amp; Misrepresentation</h2>
            <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Please ensure that any notice or counter-notice you submit is accurate and made in good faith. Knowingly submitting a false or misleading claim of infringement may render you liable for damages and legal costs, including where permitted under applicable law, and we may disclose your identity to the affected party or authorities in connection with legal proceedings.</p>
        </div>

